id: pm-rust-oracle-1118
title: Refresh published pm-cli oracle to 2026.11.18
description: "Classify the published CLI divergences, update native parity and validate the locked npm oracle on Linux."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 1
tags[6]: "gh:unbraind/pm-cli#1753","gh:unbraind/pm-cli#1754","gh:unbraind/pm-cli#1757","gh:unbraind/pm-rust#176","gh:unbraind/pm-rust#181",oracle
created_at: "2026-11-18T09:41:09.150Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-20T18:32:57.834Z"
author: codex-sol
parent: pm-rust-u4al
comments[68]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-18T09:41:20.010Z",codex-sol,Started from the Dependabot head. npm latest is 2026.11.18. Reviewing the failed matrix and reproducing against the current pin.
  "2026-11-18T09:57:01.888Z",codex-sol,"All seven failed jobs in run 44015087729 report two cases. GH-1707 in 2026.11.13 introduces credential-bearing identity admission and stored-holder redaction. Direct 2026.11.18 probes confirm stored holders are redacted without requiring credential restoration from a clean invocation. The full Linux run also confirms GH-1684 and GH-1703 in 2026.11.14 change TOON receipts and budgeted row counts, and GH-1336 in 2026.11.16 adds claim activity evidence. Implementing these wire changes while the remaining suites run."
  "2026-11-18T10:10:24.585Z",codex-sol,"Published 2026.11.18 accepts the unchanged replay at the old TOON overhead boundary. The same stale-output-cursor defect remains at an adjacent second-projection boundary, with successful replay on either side. Saved an upstream draft after checking related issues. Native already had this stale replay behavior. Kept the existing reprojected-snapshot test and tracked the separate GH-1336 takeover and next write/read work under pm-rust-stale-claim-takeover."
  "2026-11-18T10:15:01.342Z",codex-sol,"GH-1706 in 2026.11.14 is another intended change exposed past the original CI stop. Published CLI probes confirm automatic expired session-lease reclamation and stale_lock_requires_override for a retained item lease. Adopted typed lock guidance and post-commit attribution warnings, plus the GH-1724 nonzero context ownership and idle counts."
  "2026-11-18T10:16:23.222Z",codex-sol,The current Linux format and all-target Clippy gates pass. The published .18 stored-holder comparison and the updated TOON budget and continuation boundary cases passed their focused runs. The full Linux and ownership matrix runs are in progress. Opening the superseding PR as a draft while those gates complete.
  "2026-11-18T10:26:43.095Z",codex-sol,"Opened draft PR 181 at 9ac32be. Its first CI run passed tracker policy, release quality and quick crash checks. Quick Rust identified the outdated release-I/O assertion and context advisory alias mismatch. Both are corrected. The published claim/holder/session lease focused cases passed 3 of 3, the advisory alias oracle test passed, and all 20 refusal unit tests passed. The native list now reconstructs its second projection to replay the emitted cursor; the regression test verifies that changing the source still refuses."
  "2026-11-18T10:50:00.886Z",codex-sol,"At 6920d21, the local Linux unit suites passed all 458 library and 83 CLI tests. The next CI run exposed a context budget mismatch and one optional usage-feedback warning in the ownership fixture. The documented 2026.11.14 UTF-16 compaction suffix now matches the published context output at budgets 100, 1000 and 1200, and the real-copy oracle test passed. The mutation fixture disables unrelated usage feedback. The 2026.11.12 GH-1700 and 2026.11.14 GH-1716 linked-test and artifact receipts and note policy are implemented, with six direct published file comparisons and four focused unit and oracle regressions passing."
  "2026-11-18T10:53:45.626Z",codex-sol,"The native linked-test removal receipt now matches the published CLI byte for byte. The focused SDK linked-note refusal test verifies both authoritative files stay byte-identical and confirms explicit append returns only the edited link. Formatting, Clippy and the focused context and list cursor checks pass. The all-target Linux and broad collection runs remain in progress. PR 154 depends on these overlapping changes landing first."
  "2026-11-18T10:59:34.155Z",codex-sol,"Exact ac3ab0c CI exposed one stale bare-ellipsis assertion in the surrogate-preservation unit. Updated the assertion for the published UTF-16 count. All 59 ownership differential tests passed locally. The published 2026.11.18 linked-note append treats a requested phrase already present across adjacent semicolon-delimited parts as unchanged, which the native SDK now preserves on retries."
  "2026-11-18T11:02:16.069Z",codex-sol,"The same CI run passed all 38 orientation oracle tests. Its ownership acceptance test still expected release to exit after committing the item, so updated it to verify the documented 2026.11.14 success receipt, its warning and its retry advice with the on-disk state assertions preserved."
  "2026-11-18T11:04:49.166Z",codex-sol,"Locally, all 11 ownership SDK acceptance cases passed with the updated release assertion. The ac3ab0c linked collection oracle completed with zero differences across its fixtures. A further probe verified the published test command rejects the artifact-only note-conflict flag before mutating linked tests. Native now rejects it too, and the full collection oracle includes that command in both renderers."
  "2026-11-18T11:08:37.045Z",codex-sol,All 459 library tests passed after updating the compaction expectation and linked-note retry case. The linked ownership acceptance command passed under pm test with progress. Formatting and all-target Clippy passed. The unsupported linked-test flag now matches the published refusal byte for byte in text and JSON and leaves the item and journal unchanged.
  "2026-11-18T11:22:50.277Z",codex-sol,At cd70569 all three platform shard-two Rust jobs and coverage shard two passed. Shard one found three legacy CLI fixtures attempting to create forbidden identities via the modern claim path. Direct comparisons with 2026.11.18 confirmed broader whole-value masking for some previously stored holders. The CLI refusal now masks the holder and detail with that rule while retaining the existing protection for copied sensitive text. Legacy fixtures seed older durable data directly.
  "2026-11-18T11:24:02.658Z",codex-sol,Tracked the remaining raw direct-SDK error projection under pm-rust-sdk-holder-projection. The CLI applies whole-value masking before rendering while supporting its existing copied-text protections.
  "2026-11-18T11:26:45.144Z",codex-sol,"The whole-value legacy holder refusal now matches published JSON byte for byte. Both focused legacy holder CLI cases pass, and the complete public prose close-recovery corpus passed with the updated fixtures. Formatting and all-target Clippy passed. The full published collection comparison passed, and the isolated session-attribution differential passed after its concurrent Linux failure."
  "2026-11-18T11:34:29.424Z",codex-sol,Exact e3e057f Ubuntu CI reached mutation acceptance after passing the 41 CLI dispatch tests. A stale SDK assertion assumed unreadable history would prevent the foreign claim refusal. The published 2026.11.18 CLI and native CLI return byte-identical already_claimed_by receipts with history_unreadable true and stale false for the synthetic directory case. Updated the acceptance test to verify the typed fallback and unchanged item and to retain the separate journal recovery assertions.
  "2026-11-18T11:41:20.514Z",codex-sol,"The GH-1710 root cursor fix is present in the published oracle. Its long producer cursor matches native and replays in both implementations. The same release family over-applies cursor preservation to item fields with those names. Synthetic 2026.11.11 and 2026.11.18 CLI comparisons and a one-field control confirm the newer version omits rows at the tight budget. The draft captures this distinct regression. Native keeps nested data compactable, with deliberate divergence at the tight budget and byte parity at the wider budget."
  "2026-11-18T11:47:14.156Z",codex-sol,"All 41 dispatch cases, 29 mutation acceptance cases, and both generated output-parity cases passed locally. The three focused pagination cases passed against the pinned oracle. In particular, both CLIs deliver byte-identical exit-2 receipts for the full triage query at the default effective cap. Both upstream draft reproductions were run from their exact saved code and yielded their passing controls."
  "2026-11-18T12:11:57.309Z",codex-sol,"At 1caff0a all six Rust jobs passed. Both coverage shards passed, and CI run 44297971605 computed 99.4681 percent lines, 99.6641 functions, 99.3810 regions and 98.0291 branches. The aggregate requires 100 percent in each dimension. Tracked under pm-rust-oracle-1118-coverage. The local Linux all-target run passed the first unit suites, all 59 ownership oracle cases and all 41 CLI dispatch cases. PR 154 still awaits the overlapping changes on main."
  "2026-11-18T12:24:10.308Z",codex-sol,PR 181 supersedes the earlier refresh PR. Linked the existing native guards to upstream pm-cli issues 1753 and 1754 after checking both reports.
  "2026-11-18T14:32:08.366Z",codex-sol,"Round CE verified the published pm-cli 2026.11.18 behavior for claims, history recovery, linked notes, and refusals. The local strict merged coverage gate passes at 100% across all four dimensions. Native tests and source comments reference unbraind/pm-cli#1753 and #1754 for the published regressions. Linked-note diagnostic wording and flag admission differences are tracked separately in pm-rust-linked-note-diagnostics."
  "2026-11-18T16:39:25.325Z",codex-sol,Reviewing the assigned PR 181 findings against native behavior and the pinned oracle. Regression tests and gate results will be linked here.
  "2026-11-18T16:52:35.107Z",codex-sol,"PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65CD-P - Retained oracle parity. In 2026.11.18 buildContextSummaryExtras counts progress among activeItems, while the two advisory counts come from inProgressWork. The native custom progress fixture exercises that distinction."
  "2026-11-18T16:52:46.341Z",codex-sol,PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65CD9f - Retained oracle parity. The pinned real CLI returned invalid_argument_value for explicit --author and PM_AUTHOR credentials. In both cases next_steps includes restore before replay followed by the plain-name replacement instruction.
  "2026-11-18T17:13:04.054Z",codex-sol,PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65CD89 - 34d1ea82c7af. Verify the finalized projection on stale-cursor recovery. Reprojected cursor replay checks the wire budget and the over-budget test requires an omission receipt.
  "2026-11-18T17:13:08.789Z",codex-sol,PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65CD9H - 34d1ea82c7af. Compose the aggregate status from release. The test reopens between steps and checks both snapshots and the aggregate.
  "2026-11-18T17:13:22.451Z",codex-sol,PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65CD-L - 34d1ea82c7af. Compute ranking recency and advisory activity from one per-item history read. Read counters exercise ordinary and terminal progress cases.
  "2026-11-18T17:13:31.427Z",codex-sol,"PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65CD-u - 34d1ea82c7af. Reject impossible omission prefixes, counts and arithmetic overflow. The unit corpus includes canonical forms and a 30000-digit count."
  "2026-11-18T17:13:37.183Z",codex-sol,"PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65CD-4 - 34d1ea82c7af. Require a present null placeholder in each grouped absent_rows coordinate. The invalid table regression rejects populated, missing and out-of-bounds cells."
  "2026-11-18T17:13:45.673Z",codex-sol,"PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65CD_S - 34d1ea82c7af. Capture each implementation's item, history and session before refusal. Stale claim and credential differentials compare against their own snapshots."
  "2026-11-18T17:13:49.428Z",codex-sol,PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65CD_e - 34d1ea82c7af. Give the malformed history timestamp a qualifying compact-baseline operation and assert the resulting advisory counts.
  "2026-11-18T17:13:53.808Z",codex-sol,"PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65CD_q - 34d1ea82c7af. Assert the unknown and idle items independently, including their separate ownership counts."
  "2026-11-18T17:13:57.545Z",codex-sol,PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65CD_7 - 34d1ea82c7af. Assert the literal restore template and each expected group independently of the TOON projection helper.
  "2026-11-18T17:14:03.103Z",codex-sol,"PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65CEAO - 34d1ea82c7af. Require the null padding key to exist, retain the explicit-null control and verify the restored rows."
  "2026-11-18T17:29:44.993Z",codex-sol,The timestamp regression also includes an older operation-free history record. It must remain ineligible for idle evidence while the compact-baseline timestamp is parsed.
  "2026-11-18T18:06:57.845Z",codex-sol,Extended the recovered-page regression to cover the explicit output budget as well as the intent budget. Both over-budget paths discard the rows and return the corresponding recovery receipt.
  "2026-11-18T18:09:11.469Z",codex-sol,"Round CK addressed 20 findings and retained six behaviors from pm-cli 2026.11.18. The merged LLVM report passed the unmodified strict check with 20534/20534 lines, 2115/2115 functions, 33603/33603 regions and 4688/4688 branches. All eight affected oracle tests, formatting, Clippy and changelog validation passed. A wider run encountered a five-second dependency-packet timeout; the direct fixture returned matching bytes across all six measurements."
  "2026-11-18T22:16:06.246Z",codex-sol,"Round CT maps Greptile PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65H_CX to feab9220af035cf6df9c2b329abe28e8b98fed14. Session publication drops the cleanup gate before its owner receipt, so the successor can reclaim a confirmed dead writer. The Linux SIGKILL regression reproduced the release attribution warning on f51fe8e and now verifies warning-free release and an updated active-work list. The two retained first-fsync cases, formatting, Clippy with warnings denied, 504 library tests, 11 ownership contracts, 61 claim/release differentials against pm-cli 2026.11.18, and changelog verification passed. The full four-dimension coverage run is in progress."
  "2026-11-19T01:34:38.094Z",codex-sol,"Round CW maps PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65PThx to 61a359c634ddf702e687fbab278d7cf1a98152ee. SDK append and replace retries target the selected tracker with overlapping IDs. The published 2026.11.18 SDK already includes --pm-path when given pmRoot, and the native CLI matches its explicit and implicit CLI refusal bytes. PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65PTh5 maps to 61a359c634ddf702e687fbab278d7cf1a98152ee and unbraind/pm-cli#1753. At budget 1000 with padding 136, unchanged native replay succeeds and the published SDK refuses read_output_cursor_stale, which the known-exception test requires. PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65PTh9 maps to 61a359c634ddf702e687fbab278d7cf1a98152ee. A future composed close timestamp refuses before any item or history write. PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65PTiD maps to 61a359c634ddf702e687fbab278d7cf1a98152ee. The dispatch regression asserts its Codex session principal under inherited Claude markers. Formatting, Clippy, changelog, 582 affected tests, the inherited-marker regression, and 960 instrumented tests passed. The full LLVM profiles and two focused supplemental tests passed the exact thresholds with 20579/20579 lines, 2116/2116 functions, 33663/33663 regions and 4692/4692 branches."
  "2026-11-19T03:10:56.926Z",codex-sol,"Round DC maps all five findings to dfaf09908daf43275b7a3512e9d571b58c58d9e7.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65Sw16 carries the original operand directory in the SDK retry. Append and replace replay from another workspace now update the original nested links and remove only the original selectors. Native and published 2026.11.18 CLI refusals from a nested directory match byte for byte and retain the original relative CLI arguments.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65Sw1_ gives SDK callers manual guidance to supply the original note again when the command would be rewritten by credential redaction. Both CLIs exit 4, redact the note, omit structured retry fields, and retain the published diagnostic next steps.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65Sw2F gives manual restoration guidance for unrepresentable relative and absolute tracker scopes. The published CLI exits 3 with tracker_root_missing when passed the original non-UTF-8 scope.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65Sw2K tells callers that the item change was saved and session attribution needs another attempt after the native publication gate clears. The regression checks the prior snapshot, the committed claim, and successful attribution on retry. Ordinary session lock contention keeps the existing guidance.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65Sw2N records the tracked exception in unbraind/pm-cli#1754. At budget 2000 native returns the compacted row and the oracle exits 2 with result_omitted true and strings_compacted false. Both return the full values at budget 20000.\nFormatting, Clippy, changelog, 506 library tests, 63 binary tests under instrumentation, 47 dispatch tests, 11 ownership contracts, and the affected 2026.11.18 oracle regression cases passed. The strict local merge of verified baseline and fresh affected profiles has 20626/20626 lines, 2119/2119 functions, 33721/33721 regions and 4700/4700 branches. Broader differential runs are in progress."
  "2026-11-19T05:00:36.140Z",codex-sol,"Round DH verified all six findings on 5793090.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65Ty4P maps to 87be2bc and 03c05c1. SDK retries name pm-rust. The published 2026.11.18 CLI rejects --artifact-cwd, --timestamp and docs --append-stable, and ordinary scoped note refusals match byte for byte.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65UOei maps to 87be2bc and 03c05c1. Both native override repairs keep the selected tracker and operand directory when replayed elsewhere.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65UOe3 and PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65Ty4T map to 87be2bc and the fixture in e29da89. Saved forced releases and ranked unassigned claims advise reconciling only the affected session attribution against current ownership.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65UOeo maps to 87be2bc. The native session publication fence waits up to 250 ms and revalidates the lease. The published 2026.11.18 fence also waited through the 75 ms contention probe.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65UOev maps to 87be2bc and e29da89. A parent-directory sync failure after rename preserves the release and reports visible session state with unknown durability. The pinned published writer ends at rename.\nFormatting, Clippy with warnings denied, changelog, 510 library tests, 63 binary tests, 61 claim/release oracle tests, 19 collections and search oracle tests, 47 dispatch tests and 11 ownership contracts passed. Three child launches failed during the first concurrent library rebuild and passed in isolation and in the clean library runs. The rebuilt LLVM mappings with merged raw profiles passed the strict gate at 20727/20727 lines, 2134/2134 functions, 33845/33845 regions and 4708/4708 branches."
  "2026-11-19T08:35:05.101Z",codex-sol,"Round DK maps PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65V4nw and PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65V4n2 to e2f4c7322d3dd0471f15bdb512b17f036c0b5fed. The SDK captures an absolute normalized artifact directory for both the original operands and its retry, including when the caller supplies a dot. Native CLI resolves the full override before anchoring, so a relative path that leaves and reenters the project anchors the same way as a direct subdirectory. Regression tests cover retry argument rendering, replay, invalid directories and direct versus parent-relative CLI anchoring. Formatting, Clippy with warnings denied, changelog, 17 collection unit tests, 48 dispatch tests and 19 differential tests with published pm-cli 2026.11.18 passed. The LLVM report merged fresh affected profiles with the verified baseline on the rebuilt maps and passed all four unchanged thresholds: 20756/20756 lines, 2137/2137 functions, 33882/33882 regions and 4710/4710 branches."
  "2026-11-19T10:54:45.353Z",codex-sol,"Round DN maps PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65Z9DQ, PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65Z9DN, PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65Z9Da and PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65Z9Dd to 7edc630cfb6a097fc85c7589cb5fb86ced8fb3fe. Published pm-cli 2026.11.18 resolves the SDK cwd through chdir, reproducing parent-link removal for an outside-pointing project symlink. Its explicit vendor/source.rs removal preserves source.rs, and the Rust SDK now matches that receipt and the item and history bytes when given the logical vendor base. Published SDK cwd rejects an existing file with ENOTDIR. The native artifact-cwd override now refuses the equivalent operation before writing. Replacing the published session lease produces lock_lost and an attribution warning while preserving both the saved claim and prior session bytes. Native lease loss now uses the existing publication conflict and directs the caller to reconcile only session attribution. The files and docs differentials compare both complete conflict rows with the oracle. Formatting, Clippy with warnings denied, and changelog passed. All 49 dispatch, 11 ownership contract, 18 refreshed collections unit, 17 refreshed session-filtered unit, and 10 collection and linked-note differential cases passed. The coverage union fixtures passed. The report merged the verified Round DK profiles with fresh candidate executions against rebuilt all-target maps and reached 20772/20772 lines, 2138/2138 functions, 33906/33906 regions and 4716/4716 branches."
  "2026-11-19T12:53:33.729Z",codex-sol,"Round DS started for Greptile thread PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65cs2Q on 48b8c06. I will verify the published CLI and SDK, exercise root and subdirectory aliases with both links present, preserve the logical base for links pointing outside, and run the package gates."
  "2026-11-19T12:55:18.551Z",codex-sol,Published pm-cli 2026.11.18 CLI and SDK each remove source.rs from an external root alias and sub/source.rs from an external subdirectory alias when both links are stored. The planned resolver accepts canonical project descendants and retains the logical suffix through an ancestor when the full directory resolves outside.
  "2026-11-19T12:56:48.689Z",codex-sol,The new differential reproduces the wrong retained link on 48b8c06 for an external alias into sub. The resolver now accepts the nearest canonical ancestor inside the project while preserving the suffix if the full directory points outside. All requested gates are running against the edited worktree.
  "2026-11-19T13:04:39.607Z",codex-sol,"Both alias targets and the existing outside-pointing symlink passed against the published oracle. The targeted branch report identified an unexercised canonicalization error, so the root-alias unit fixture now also verifies that a missing descendant keeps its logical suffix."
  "2026-11-19T13:09:25.159Z",codex-sol,"The strict LLVM merge against the rebuilt all-target maps passed at 20773/20773 lines, 2138/2138 functions, 33908/33908 regions and 4718/4718 branches. It used the verified Round DN profile archive plus fresh Round DS collection unit and alias differential profiles. Only the collections source coverage totals changed. The separate fresh all-target run is still in progress."
  "2026-11-19T13:10:28.418Z",codex-sol,"Round DS maps Greptile thread PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65cs2Q to 58e939027dad10fb92015a493fbb4c8253fdb46a. External aliases to the project root or a subdirectory now remove the corresponding stored link. The regression verifies the exact published removal receipt and durable bytes for both alias targets, and the existing outside-pointing symlink case remains covered."
  "2026-11-19T13:13:20.791Z",codex-sol,The supplemental fresh coverage run had three self-spawning library fixtures return ENOENT after a concurrent focused rebuild replaced their running executable. The process executable was marked deleted. All three passed on individual reruns from the stable rebuilt executable. The independent strict merged coverage gate remained green.
  "2026-11-19T13:31:32.432Z",codex-sol,"Round DS local gates passed against published pm-cli 2026.11.18. Formatting, all-target Clippy with warnings denied, changelog, and both coverage union tests passed. The required Cargo suites passed 513 library, 49 CLI dispatch, 11 ownership, 61 claim/release differential, and 21 search/collections differential cases. The claim/release test name inventory matched the union of its 23 initial and 38 continuation passes. Strict merged coverage reached 100 percent in all four dimensions. The supplemental fresh all-target run was stopped after the independent merged gate passed and the three interrupted self-spawning fixtures passed individually."
  "2026-11-19T16:22:18.970Z",codex-sol,Round DZ started on the synchronized PR head. Reviewing all 15 threads against the pinned published CLI and the Rust SDK contract before changing behavior.
  "2026-11-19T16:31:17.512Z",codex-sol,"Round DZ oracle probes confirmed separate hyphen-leading notes, stale lock reclamation for an unowned pause, per-attempt lock expiry, and projection of encoded identity credentials copied into recovery fields. The native SDK now preserves absolute restore scope and logical artifact paths. The Rust year-boundary test records the published extended ISO date alongside the native null fallback. Local gates are running."
  "2026-11-19T18:22:03.625Z",codex-sol,"Round DZ review of pm-rust#181 at 516d391 against pm-cli 2026.11.18. All 15 findings apply.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65d2tN — native_note_repair_replays_only_in_the_selected_tracker and linked_note_recovery_matches_published_semantics. The oracle accepts a separate hyphen-leading note, and the native retry retains that grammar and the following flags.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65d2tU — sdk_collection_reads_ignore_the_artifact_base. SDK listing and linked-test operations ignore unused directories, including an empty path.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65d2tX — collection_restore_after_removal_is_read_only and cli_omitted_rows_retain_tracker_root_as_invocation_directory. SDK restores use the selected absolute tracker and replay from another tracker with the same ID. CLI relative and non-UTF-8 guidance are verified separately.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65d2ta — private_sdk_principals_refuse_before_storage. Explicit and scoped invalid principals refuse before forced pause can modify item, history or session bytes. The published CLI rejects the corresponding invalid author before mutation.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65d2tn — claim_eligibility_handles_the_utc_year_boundary. The pinned oracle reports +010000-01-01T00:30:00.000Z across the boundary. Native gives null outside its UTC range and matches the in-range value.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65d2tx — ownership_session_faults_and_contention_preserve_durable_steps. Both implementations save the release on lock contention. The oracle says nothing needs a retry. Native now directs callers to check and reconcile only session attribution after the lock clears.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65d2t1 — stale_session_lock_lifecycle_matches_published_bytes. Owned and unowned pause, claim, release and start each assert stale lock removal in both trackers.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65d2t6 — reclaimed_session_writer_cannot_replace_new_attribution. A disconnected channel aborts publication and leaves the session unchanged. Successor publication still fences the old writer.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65d2uB — session_publication_waits_for_transient_cleanup_gate. The publisher releases the fixture gate only after observing actual contention. The next acquisition publishes the snapshot.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65kcQN — artifact_cwd_file_refusal_preserves_item_and_history and artifact_cwd_resolves_root_alias_without_following_its_suffix. A regular file in the base or its ancestry refuses before any write, and a missing directory still anchors the link. The flag is native-only.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65kcQU — project_alias_removal_preserves_internal_directory_symlinks. Project-root alias and direct logical removal select the same stored path. An alias directly into a project subdirectory also remains usable.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65kcQb — projected_collection_recovery_keeps_the_selected_binary and encoded_identity_projection_preserves_native_recovery. Redaction covers copies of encoded identity credentials while retaining public message text. The published CLI also protects the copied fixture.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65kcQj — session_acquisition_refreshes_the_clock_on_retry. Deterministic samples prove an initially live lease expires within the wait and the new receipt uses the successful attempt's clock, matching the oracle's per-attempt policy.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65kcQp — recency_honors_event_classes_and_legacy_paths plus the orientation differential. Established event classes take precedence, and the fallback uses borrowed paths with the existing maintenance and malformed-path behavior.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65kcQ2 — projected_collection_recovery_keeps_the_selected_binary and encoded_identity_projection_preserves_native_recovery. Projected recovery retains pm-rust for its native-only flag and pm for published arguments.\n\nGate evidence\nFormatting, deny-warnings Clippy, changelog check and both profile-union fixtures passed.\nThe standard Rust unit, binary, CLI dispatch, ownership, claim/release, search/collections and orientation cases passed across the full run and focused retries. Final full unit rerun passed 519 library and 63 binary tests. The existing five-second dependency packet deadline recurred during concurrent runs, then the unchanged case passed in isolation. This behavior is tracked in pm-rust-local-packet-deadline.\nThe final mapping and merged LLVM profiles passed all four unchanged thresholds: 20812/20812 lines, 2147/2147 functions, 33990/33990 regions, and 4726/4726 branch outcomes. The full instrumented run and final instrumented regressions supplied the profiles."
  "2026-11-19T19:52:13.727Z",codex-sol,Round EC started on 6411f35 after reading all five review threads. The pinned SDK distinguishes strict ownership history from advisory activity and recognizes stored event classes. Verifying native retry spelling and both history paths with regression fixtures.
  "2026-11-19T21:18:09.145Z",codex-sol,"Round EC reviewed all five pm-rust#181 threads at 6411f35 against the locked pm-cli 2026.11.18 CLI and SDK.\n\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65qOPE — native_note_repair_replays_only_in_the_selected_tracker executes append and replace with --message=-draft and verifies the saved history message. linked_note_recovery_matches_published_semantics verifies the published two-argument spelling.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65qOPO — claim_history_provenance_and_activity_match_published checks that an array context and a null receipt make ownership history unreadable and the holder ineligible for a stale verdict. Legacy receipts and explicit null activity remain readable.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65qOPW — advisory_history_activity_matches_published checks that activity skips malformed shape, including a recent update without a patch, and still accepts valid records.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65qOPe — advisory_history_activity_matches_published checks that malformed retained activity falls back to the baseline timestamp and explicit null contributes no prefix activity.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65qOPr — both history regressions check that stored maintenance and substantive classes override paths. The advisory regression also checks that an unknown class falls back to path classification.\n\nFormatting, deny-warnings Clippy, changelog, and both LLVM profile-union fixtures passed. The required published-oracle Rust targets passed across 520 library, 50 CLI dispatch, 11 ownership, 61 claim/release, 21 search/collections, and 38 orientation tests. The clean library rerun recovered six subprocess fixture failures from a concurrent test executable rebuild.\nThe instrumented run used an earlier retry fixture for search/collections. The corrected oracle and native regression passed on rerun, and the merged profile gate passed with 20846/20846 lines, 2150/2150 functions, 34041/34041 regions, and 4726/4726 branch outcomes."
  "2026-11-20T00:33:11.697Z",codex-sol,"Round EG maps all five findings on 073f293 to the commit titled Fix Round EG collection and release recovery.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65ux6H - The 2026.11.18 oracle refuses --note --json with exit 2 and unchanged item and history bytes. It accepts --note -draft and --note=--json. The native parser and differential tests cover those value boundaries.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65ux6L - The oracle reports unknown_option for --artifact-cwd. The native-only option refuses a missing directory value before writing, accepts the attached literal --artifact-cwd=--json, and accepts missing/sub.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65ux6R - The oracle requires the attached form for the hyphen-leading author. Both native note-repair policies now replay with --author=-fixture, with the author verified in history.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65ux6S - The oracle accepts item docs, item files, and item test. Native dispatch now replays those namespaces from its recovery instructions.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65ux6Z - The oracle saves release ownership and history despite a session I/O failure. The native receipt keeps the saved release and directs reconciliation of session attribution after the failure is fixed.\nThe required stable Rust suites passed against the pinned npm oracle. Formatting, deny-warning Clippy, the changelog check, and the merged LLVM coverage gate passed. Lines, functions, regions, and branches all reached 100 percent."
  "2026-11-20T04:06:11.878Z",codex-sol,"Round EM verified all four pm-rust#181 findings at 2228b77 against the published pm-cli 2026.11.18 CLI and SDK. The fixes and regression tests are in Fix Round EM ownership refusals and attribution.\n\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65yq-c - The oracle refuses an abandoned empty or whitespace-only receipt with stale_lock_requires_override and reports lock_conflict while the gate is held. Native acquisition now makes the stale decision under the gate, gives owner-verified removal guidance for unreadable receipts, and preserves the lock and the item until an authorized retry. Differential tests cover gate contention, abandoned receipts, and forced recovery.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65yq-e - The pinned SDK leaves stale eligibility intact for a well-formed workspace comment with an invalid timestamp. Workspace fixtures compare the entire activity receipt and retain conservative evidence for unreadable JSON, undated restores and rewrites, and invalid compactions.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65yq-i - The published SDK saves a claim under a held session lock and the session stays as it was after the lock clears. The native saved-claim receipt now directs attribution reconciliation. The composed-start test asserts the revised advice and compares the remaining receipt and durable bytes against the oracle.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65yq-j - The oracle preserves --author beta when a stored holder supplied the credential. Native projection preserves the declared flag in normalized_args, provided_fields, and the rebuilt attempted command. The regression also checks redaction of separate and attached credential-bearing values.\n\nFormatting, deny-warnings Clippy, changelog, and both coverage profile-union fixtures passed. The required stable suites passed across the full run and focused rerun of the updated fixtures, with 522 library, 64 binary unit, 53 CLI dispatch, 12 ownership contract, 64 claim/release differential, and 22 search/collections differential cases. The full merged coverage run is in progress at the unchanged four-dimension threshold of 100 percent."
  "2026-11-20T05:57:13.041Z",codex-sol,"Round ER started against PR #181 head 5070345. Read all seven review threads. Checking the published 2026.11.18 settings, history, refusal and force behavior alongside the Rust paths. Preserving Round EC, EG and EM option parsing and retry behavior."
  "2026-11-20T07:32:56.011Z",codex-sol,"Round ER on 5070345 against the published pm-cli 2026.11.18. All seven findings are addressed by Fix Round ER history evidence and refusal redaction.\n\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs651ruq — Strict ownership reproduced in both implementations: session A receives the note conflict, session B receives ownership_conflict on the retry, and session A successfully appends. Rust guidance names the original detected session and the original SDK AuthorIdentity while retaining the executable commands.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs651rut — Native recency checks string paths in supplied patch rows using the same validation as claim activity. Existing legacy records without a patch retain the published recency behavior. The pinned context command exits with unknown_error for a malformed row. Native skips it and retains older valid evidence.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs651ruw — The pinned loader accepts 72.0 and 24e0 as whole hours and rejects fractional, nonpositive and out-of-range values. Both CLIs create byte-identical item and history records with the accepted values.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs651ru1 — The claim-activity differential matches the published stale verdict and receipt for a date-only claim at UTC midnight and for an invalid calendar month.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs651ru5 — Public Rust redaction projects arrays and scalars in place, preserves null and applies recovery metadata to object envelopes.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs651ru8 — Public Rust redaction registers the stored holder before projecting a copied value, without raw arguments or CLI projection scope. Synthetic literal and encoded fixtures preserve declared flags, project option values and remove unsafe retries.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs651ru- — The abandoned receipt fixture now requires both CLIs to exit successfully after --force and verifies alpha as the persisted assignee.\n\nOpen follow-ups are pm-rust-oracle-malformed-recency for the pinned context failure and pm-rust-orientation-stale-evidence for native context idle settings and dates.\n\nFinal validation passed formatting, deny-warnings Clippy, changelog and both LLVM profile union fixtures. The pinned stable suites accounted for all 780 tests: 526 library, 64 binary, 53 CLI dispatch, 12 ownership, 65 claim and release, 22 search and collections, and 38 orientation. The known dependency-packet five-second deadline failed in concurrent runs and passed unchanged in both single-test reruns. The current LLVM mapping and refreshed profiles passed the merged gate at 20990/20990 lines, 2167/2167 functions, 34304/34304 regions and 4766/4766 branch outcomes."
  "2026-11-20T10:08:15.580Z",codex-sol,"Round EV started on the open PR head 9816f48. Read all five review threads and confirmed the help, timestamp, threshold, and retry paths under review. The pinned oracle and existing parser regressions are the comparison points."
  "2026-11-20T11:44:34.429Z",codex-sol,"Round EV verified all five findings on 9816f48 against the pinned pm-cli 2026.11.18 CLI and SDK. The fixes and regression tests are in 7b2b723.\n\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs655Ag8 — Linked-test help omits --note-conflict, files and docs help still show it, and a linked-test add with the flag still returns the published unknown_option receipt.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs655AhA — Claim eligibility now matches the SDK through the inclusive Date limit. The 100000000-hour claim returns +013434-07-19T02:06:30.183Z. The differential compares the native receipt directly, including signed extended years and a result one millisecond past the limit.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs655AhE — Context uses the shared stored-activity timestamp parser. At 2026-11-05T00:00:00Z, the date-only history case previously counted one idle item and now matches the oracle's zero. The evaluation clock still requires RFC 3339.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs655AhH — The shared whole-hour decoder treats 24, 24.0 and 24e0 alike. The 30-hour fixture counts as idle with all three spellings, matching the oracle.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs655AhK — The session retry-clock unit test uses a bounded wait hook. It keeps the immediate zero-budget conflict, permits one controlled retry, and verifies the timestamp in the written receipt.\n\nThe idle-evidence outcome is also recorded on pm-rust-orientation-stale-evidence and pm-rust-oracle-malformed-recency. The separate malformed-patch failure remains tracked there. In the pinned package, the legacy classifier throws TypeError for a missing path while the stale-work reader skips the same row.\n\nFormatting, deny-warnings Clippy, changelog and the two LLVM union fixtures passed. The pinned stable gates accounted for 782 tests across lib, bin, CLI dispatch, ownership, claim/release, orientation and search/collections, plus 29 mutation-contract tests. The known five-second packet deadline recurred twice under concurrent load and passed at its unchanged limit in the final isolated stable run. All 39 orientation tests passed in the instrumented shard. The eligibility addition-overflow case passed in both builds.\n\nBoth instrumented shards passed. The verified union of 3486 raw profiles plus the focused addition-overflow profile reached 21007/21007 lines, 2169/2169 functions, 34347/34347 regions and 4772/4772 branch outcomes."
  "2026-11-20T13:29:26.284Z",codex-sol,"Round EZ started on df2f418. Verify the eleven review threads against the pinned published CLI and run the regression, lint, changelog, and merged coverage gates."
  "2026-11-20T13:36:17.905Z",codex-sol,"The pinned CLI stores -mreviewed literally after --note, so the parser retains the existing behavior. It accepts --note=--json and rejects the separate form. The symlink-parent case reproduced against both executables. The asserted SDK repair retains the original principal by directing callers to retry with the original identity. Validation is running."
  "2026-11-20T14:28:04.942Z",codex-sol,The instrumented mutation contract exposed another historical timestamp in a live-lock fixture. Updated the affected mutation and collection fixtures to stamp the lease with the current time and kept the historical mutation timestamp. All 29 native mutation contract tests pass. Coverage resumed after excluding the previous profiles for the changed targets.
  "2026-11-20T14:41:56.311Z",codex-sol,"Round EZ reviewed all eleven threads from df2f418 against pm-cli 2026.11.18 and current native code.\n\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65-3tl — 2f779f0 resolves the symlink target before parent traversal. The oracle run from link/.. and the native artifact-cwd run both remove vendor/source.rs and retain source.rs.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65-3tp — 2f779f0 directs callers to an SDK repair with the original asserted AuthorIdentity when the fallback author has a different principal. The strict-ownership regression refuses the fallback and appends with the asserted owner.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65-3ts — The oracle exits 0 and stores -mreviewed literally for both --note -mreviewed and --note=-mreviewed. 2f779f0 adds differential evidence for both inputs and preserves that parser behavior.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65-3tv — 2f779f0 writes and judges ownership leases with the wall clock while preserving the historical mutation timestamp. The oracle lock module uses nowIso() and Date.now(). dce2e43 updates the live fixtures and preserves both bounded waits and typed expiry checks.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65-3t2 — 2f779f0 matches the published Date precision. The differential fixture reports 72 idle hours and stale true at the threshold and retains the raw timestamp in the receipt.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65-3t7 — 2f779f0 preserves the parsed subcommand in normalized recovery. The oracle preserves pm claim when a stored holder name collides with claim. Native also masks the word when supplied as an argument value.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65-3uB — 2f779f0 keeps the restore warning when an independent replay example changes. A clean structurally projected invocation still receives the ordinary holder guidance.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65-3uD — 2f779f0 normalizes only the first suggestion in the published comparison and checks the remaining native suggestions for replay advice.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65-3uH — 2f779f0 checks both explicit author spellings and executes the author-free replay under the same detected session.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65-3uJ — 2f779f0 uses --note=--json in the default retry. The pinned executable refuses the separate flag-looking value and successfully applies the attached retry.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65-3uN — 2f779f0 checks assignee and claim_principal redaction in the skipped SDK claim. The original item and history bytes stay intact.\n\nThe native gates passed all 817 tests, formatting, Clippy and the changelog check. The exact coverage union is in progress. Follow-up evidence is in pm-rust-shared-lock-wall-clock and pm-rust-linked-note-diagnostics."
  "2026-11-20T15:19:47.863Z",codex-sol,"Round EZ validation completed. The strict LLVM profile union restored 3493 original profiles. Both union proof tests and the final report passed after the focused library and CLI coverage cases. Coverage is 21030/21030 lines, 2169/2169 functions, 34383/34383 regions and 4776/4776 branch outcomes. The symlink fixture passed with regular and symlinked temporary roots. The updated mutation, library and CLI fixtures passed their filtered reruns. Formatting, Clippy and changelog passed. Round coverage artifacts were removed."
  "2026-11-20T18:20:23.534Z",codex-sol,"Round FC verified all four pm-rust#181 threads from 2e24fa4 against the pinned pm-cli 2026.11.18.\n\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs66Dwpn — parser_diagnostics_project_only_actual_author_values verifies that Clap projects bare and URL-form author credentials on create and close errors. The published CLI masks the encoded author credential and its copy in the invalid priority. The native regression also checks ordinary text, a value taken by another option, the argument delimiter and a missing author value.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs66Dwpv — projected_note_conflicts_withhold_retries verifies that projected non-native conflict receipts omit both structured retry fields and give restoration guidance. The native fallback retains its original scope guidance. The published CLI likewise omits both fields for a credential-bearing note, and linked_note_retry_scope_matches_published_cli compares the full rendered refusal.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs66Dwp5 — stale_session_lock_reclamation_matches_published_policy and stale_session_lock_lifecycle_matches_published_bytes require exit 0 from both implementations and confirm that the expired lock is removed.\nPRRT_kwDOTwgMRs66Dwp7 — sdk_note_conflict_retry_preserves_the_request asserts both retry vectors against independently constructed operands. default_note_retry_replays_hyphen_notes_on_published_cli replays the suggested command against a seeded row and verifies the exact removal and append of the literal hyphen-leading note.\n\nFormatting, deny-warnings Clippy, changelog, and both profile union fixtures passed. The required stable suites passed 751 tests, including 531 library, 64 binary unit, 54 CLI dispatch, 12 ownership, 65 claim and release, and 25 search and collections cases. The CLI dispatch suite passed again after adding the close error regression. The first instrumented orientation attempt reproduced the five-second child deadline tracked by pm-rust-local-packet-deadline. The unchanged case passed in isolation and the remaining instrumented targets passed. Strict merged LLVM coverage passed with 21047/21047 lines, 2169/2169 functions, 34397/34397 regions and 4780/4780 branch outcomes."
